# Line endings. A Windows clone with core.autocrlf=true would otherwise check the
# shell scripts out with CRLF, which breaks `bash -n`, shellcheck (SC1017) and the
# shebang itself. Keep anything executed by a shell, or by `make`, LF on every OS.
* text=auto

*.sh text eol=lf
Makefile text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf

# Binary assets: never line-ending-converted, never diffed as text.
*.webp binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
